<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Triple Entente</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Triple Entente was the informal alignment of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> formed in the years before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>. It developed from the Franco-Russian alliance and Britain's agreements with France in 1904 and Russia in 1907. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a> profile treats German fears of encirclement by the Entente powers as a factor in the diplomacy and war that led to the empire's collapse.</p></div>
